 % !TeX root = ../thesis.tex
 \begin{cabstract}
-灵巧手触觉研究需要可执行的机器人示教、语义明确的多模态数据和可靠的迁移评价。几何抓取候选不必然满足整机约束，轨迹文件可读取也不代表动作与观测关系正确；同维仿真与真实触觉更不意味着物理等价。针对这些问题，本文研究灵巧手仿真示教数据构建与触觉跨域重建方法。
+灵巧手操作需要通过多指接触完成抓取、搬移与装配，示教采集涉及反复操作、物体复位和设备维护。仿真便于控制初始条件、重复执行任务并记录完整状态，为扩大示教覆盖和分析接触过程提供了实验手段。然而，抓取方案的可执行性、示教数据的时序一致性以及仿真触觉与真实触觉的差异，直接影响这些数据的使用。本文围绕上述问题，研究灵巧手仿真示教数据构建与触觉跨域重建方法。
 
-构建RM75B机械臂与途见科技自研欠驱动灵巧手的多任务仿真平台，统一机器人控制、任务执行和触觉记录，依据曲面几何建立16个Patch、712维处理后触觉观测体系，并检查指定历史任务记录。适配GraspQP官方抓取评价指标，参考DexEvolve设计实现进化搜索，结合腕部姿态扩展、可达性、碰撞约束和连续轨迹求解，形成候选生成、机器人约束筛选与专家示教验证流程，分别判定候选质量、任务结果和严格回放质量。
+构建RealMAN（睿尔曼智能）RM75B机械臂与途见科技自研欠驱动灵巧手的多任务仿真平台，集成控制、任务执行与传感器记录。根据指节、指尖和手掌的几何差异构建曲面阵列，获得16个触觉区域、712维处理后观测。在此基础上，适配GraspQP官方评价指标，参考DexEvolve设计实现进化搜索，通过腕部姿态扩展、可达性、碰撞约束和连续轨迹检查，将抓取候选转化为专家示教。Sugar Box的10条历史局部扰动记录均通过严格回放验证，验证范围为同一物体及相近源抓取。
 
-建立状态、动作、视觉与触觉的记录合同，区分位置命令与逆运动学目标、策略观测与完整仿真状态，核查动作和执行前后观测的时序配对及格式转换。通过来源追踪、数值有效性、连续性、完整性和重复关系检查，验证指定修复数据，并识别历史命令不连续与状态字段缺失问题，形成限定数据范围内的分层质量准入依据。
+针对多模态示教的记录与使用，建立状态和动作的字段定义、执行前后观测的时序配对及数据转换流程，并结合来源、数值、连续性和重复关系开展分层质量检查。指定Sugar Box修复数据的340行导出动作、状态命令区及触觉与源记录对应字段的最大绝对差均为0；同时识别出历史命令不连续和状态字段缺失问题，明确不同版本数据的适用条件。
 
-在缺少认证同步物理配对的条件下，利用真实触觉统计先验指导仿真物理探针构造伪配对，分别训练双域变分自编码器，以门控循环单元映射网络连接独立潜空间。进一步探索共享参数向量场积分、对抗优化、多视角判别和残差修正，结合分布距离、邻域覆盖、输入依赖和跨会话判别表现进行综合评价。
+针对触觉跨域差异，利用真实数据的统计先验指导仿真物理探针构造伪配对，以独立双域变分自编码器学习时序表示，并训练门控循环单元网络映射两域潜变量。进一步引入共享参数向量场积分，探索对抗优化、多视角判别和残差修正，分别检查分布距离、邻域覆盖、输入依赖与判别器的跨会话表现。
 
-实验中，潜变量映射改进版本在原冻结验证协议的11个分类器实例中仅2个联合通过。共享场初始比较基线的指定切片Wasserstein距离相对未转换仿真输入下降49.77\%，只支持有限的边际改善。对抗优化虽可使生成样本在对应判别器下的接受率达到100\%，分布质量并未同步改善；多视角残差终点发生明显距离退化，后续冻结审计亦表明当前判别器未满足既定真实域接受要求。结果揭示接受率、分布相似性、输入依赖与评价器可靠性不能相互替代。本文形成了仿真示教数据构建、触觉重建与质量诊断的探索链路，但尚未完成完整触觉仿真到现实迁移验收或真实机器人任务收益验证。
+实验表明，潜变量映射改进版本在原冻结验证协议的11个分类器实例中有2个联合通过。训练后的共享向量场单步基线在指定切片Wasserstein距离下，相对未转换仿真输入下降49.77\%。后续对抗优化的生成接受率可达100\%，但分布质量未同步改善，多视角残差终点出现明显距离退化。冻结审计进一步发现当前判别器未达到既定真实域接受要求。这些结果说明，接受率、分布相似性与输入对应关系需要分别验证。本文完成了仿真示教构建、指定数据质量验证及触觉跨域重建探索，完整触觉仿真到现实迁移与实机任务收益仍需进一步检验。
 \end{cabstract}
 
 \begin{eabstract}
-Tactile research for dexterous manipulation requires executable demonstrations, multimodal data with explicit semantics, and reliable transfer evaluation. Geometrically plausible grasps need not satisfy whole-robot constraints; readable trajectories need not preserve command-observation relationships; and equal-dimensional simulated and real tactile observations need not be physically equivalent. This thesis investigates simulation-based demonstration data construction and cross-domain tactile reconstruction.
+Dexterous manipulation relies on multi-finger contact for grasping, transport, and assembly. Collecting demonstrations requires repeated operation, object resetting, and equipment maintenance. Simulation enables controlled initial conditions, repeatable execution, and access to complete states, supporting broader demonstration coverage and contact analysis. The usefulness of these data depends on executable grasps, consistent recording, and the gap between simulated and real tactile responses. This thesis investigates simulation-based demonstration data construction and cross-domain tactile reconstruction.
 
-A multi-task platform integrates an RM75B manipulator and an underactuated dexterous hand developed by Tachin-Tech with unified control, task execution, and tactile recording. A curved sensing layout provides processed observations with 16 patches and 712 scalar channels, inspected using selected historical task records. Official GraspQP evaluation metrics are adapted, and evolutionary search is implemented with reference to DexEvolve. Wrist-pose expansion, reachability, collision constraints, and continuous trajectories connect grasp candidates to expert demonstrations. Candidate quality, task outcomes, and strict replay quality are distinguished.
+A multi-task platform integrates a RealMAN RM75B manipulator and an underactuated dexterous hand developed by Tachin-Tech, including control, task execution, and sensor recording. Curved arrays adapted to the finger segments, fingertips, and palm provide 16 sensing patches and 712 processed channels. Official GraspQP metrics are adapted, and evolutionary search is implemented with reference to DexEvolve. Wrist-pose expansion, reachability, collision constraints, and continuous-trajectory checks connect grasp candidates to expert demonstrations. Ten historical Sugar Box records with local perturbations pass strict replay verification within the scope of one object and closely related source grasps.
 
-Recording contracts separate position commands from inverse-kinematics targets and policy observations from complete simulation states. Temporal pairing and conversion are examined alongside provenance, validity, continuity, completeness, and duplication. Selected repairs are verified, while command discontinuities and missing state fields are identified in historical records, supporting layered admission within the inspected data scope.
+Multimodal recording defines state and action fields, pre-action and post-action temporal pairing, and format conversion. Layered checks examine provenance, numerical validity, continuity, and duplication. For a specified repaired Sugar Box export, the maximum absolute differences for the action, command portion of the state, and tactile fields are all zero across 340 rows relative to their corresponding source fields. Historical command discontinuities and missing state fields are also identified, establishing version-specific conditions for data use.
 
-Without certified synchronous physical pairs, real tactile statistics guide simulated probes to construct pseudo-pairs. Separate variational autoencoders learn domain-specific representations, connected by a gated recurrent unit mapping network. Shared-parameter vector fields, adversarial optimization, multi-view discrimination, and residual refinement are explored using complementary distribution, neighborhood, input-dependence, and cross-session evaluations.
+Real tactile statistics guide simulated physical probes to construct pseudo-pairs. Independent variational autoencoders learn temporal representations for the two domains, connected by a gated recurrent unit mapping network. Shared-parameter vector-field integration, adversarial optimization, multi-view discrimination, and residual refinement are then explored. Evaluation separately examines distribution distances, neighborhood coverage, input dependence, and cross-session discriminator behavior.
 
-The adapted latent mapping meets the joint requirements for only two of eleven classifier instances under the original frozen validation protocol. The initial shared-field baseline reduces the specified sliced Wasserstein distance by 49.77\% relative to unconverted simulation inputs, indicating limited marginal improvement. Adversarial optimization can achieve 100\% generated-sample acceptance under the corresponding discriminator without improving distribution quality. The multi-view residual endpoint exhibits substantial distance degradation, and a frozen audit finds that the current discriminator fails the prescribed real-domain acceptance requirement. Acceptance, distributional similarity, input dependence, and evaluator reliability are therefore not interchangeable. The resulting pipeline links simulated demonstrations, data quality control, tactile reconstruction, and diagnosis, while complete tactile sim-to-real acceptance and benefits to real-robot tasks remain unverified.
+The adapted latent mapping satisfies the joint requirements for two of eleven classifier instances under the original frozen validation protocol. The trained shared-field single-step baseline reduces the specified sliced Wasserstein distance by 49.77\% relative to unconverted simulation inputs. Subsequent adversarial optimization reaches 100\% generated-sample acceptance without corresponding distribution-quality improvement, while the multi-view residual endpoint exhibits substantial distance degradation. A frozen audit further finds that the current discriminator fails the prescribed real-domain acceptance requirement. Acceptance, distributional similarity, and input correspondence therefore require separate verification. This thesis establishes simulated demonstration construction, specified data-quality verification, and tactile reconstruction experiments; complete tactile sim-to-real transfer and real-robot task benefits require further evaluation.
 \end{eabstract}
